  "body": "Is there a plan to support parsing a URL with multiple hosts? typically used by DBs [1]\r\n\r\nit would be very convenient, possibly as an option\r\n\r\n```js\r\n\r\nconst url = 'https://foo@server1.foo.net:7998,server2.foo.net:7998,server3.foo.net:7998/data?authMechanism=X509&replicaSet=rs0&ssl=true&sslValidate=true';\r\n\r\nconst u = new URL(url);\r\n```\r\n\r\n> TypeError [ERR_INVALID_URL]: Invalid URL\r\n\r\n[1]: \r\n- postgresql: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/10/static/libpq-connect.html#LIBPQ-CONNSTRING\r\n- mongodb: https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/reference/connection-string/",
